WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.952
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:03.952 --> 00:00:06.400
TARQUIN CLARK: Finding a
job, no matter your industry,

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:07.390
can be tough.

00:00:07.390 --> 00:00:09.370
And if you're hiring,
getting your job in front

00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:13.450
of the right candidate can be
both challenging and expensive.

00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:15.640
Part of the challenge is
that there is no standard

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:17.470
for writing job postings.

00:00:17.470 --> 00:00:19.690
As companies, we often
use internal language

00:00:19.690 --> 00:00:24.070
to describe job titles that
may not be obvious to seekers.

00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:25.990
This issue is
compounded by the fact

00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:29.200
that most off-the-shelf search
technology is keyword-based,

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:31.780
focusing on the two to
three generic words that

00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:34.550
often make up job titles.

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:36.800
While keyword search is
effective at matching keywords

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:40.100
to content, it typically
fails to return good results

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:42.110
when used for job search.

00:00:42.110 --> 00:00:44.330
Cloud Job Discovery
offers access

00:00:44.330 --> 00:00:47.340
to Google's proven search and
machine learning capabilities

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:49.250
through a plug-and-play
Cloud service,

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:51.710
improving job
discoverability, job seeker

00:00:51.710 --> 00:00:54.020
experience, and conversion.

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:57.110
It's packed with functionality,
such as seniority alignment,

00:00:57.110 --> 00:00:59.680
job-related synonym
and acronym detection,

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:01.970
to improve the job
seeker experience.

00:01:01.970 --> 00:01:03.920
And we're constantly
talking to job seekers

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:07.010
to find innovative ways to
help them discover new jobs,

00:01:07.010 --> 00:01:09.890
like preferred commute
time and mode of transit.

00:01:09.890 --> 00:01:11.610
So how does it work?

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:15.890
Let's take a look at a job site
powered by Cloud Job Discovery.

00:01:15.890 --> 00:01:18.560
This could be a job board,
career site, applicant tracking

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:21.440
system, or any
other jobs property.

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:23.450
The job content on
the site is first

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:27.760
inserted into a private tenant
on the Google Cloud Platform.

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:29.840
Cloud Job Discovery
then goes to work,

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:32.390
parsing, classifying,
and mapping the content

00:01:32.390 --> 00:01:35.480
to pre-trained data models,
which codify our knowledge

00:01:35.480 --> 00:01:38.900
and understanding of
occupations, skills, education,

00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:40.610
and more.

00:01:40.610 --> 00:01:43.130
Here's a visual representation
of our title data

00:01:43.130 --> 00:01:47.540
model, which contains over
254,000 normalized titles, each

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:51.230
belonging to one of 30
top-level categories.

00:01:51.230 --> 00:01:54.140
This knowledge enables us to
return not just the correct

00:01:54.140 --> 00:01:58.820
role for each job seeker, but
also similar roles nearby.

00:01:58.820 --> 00:02:00.580
When job seekers
search on the site,

00:02:00.580 --> 00:02:02.840
we apply machine learning
to truly understand

00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:05.810
the intent of the query,
and then retrieve, rank,

00:02:05.810 --> 00:02:07.970
and return highly
relevant results that

00:02:07.970 --> 00:02:11.330
continue to improve over time.

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:14.030
Hiring companies with career
sites powered by Cloud Job

00:02:14.030 --> 00:02:16.250
Discovery, such as
Johnson &amp; Johnson,

00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:18.590
have seen remarkable
increases in career site

00:02:18.590 --> 00:02:20.960
engagement and
candidate conversion,

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:23.730
especially on
hard-to-fill roles.

00:02:23.730 --> 00:02:25.700
Job boards and applicant
tracking systems

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:28.730
using Cloud Job Discovery,
such as CareerBuilder,

00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:30.560
are also seeing
increased engagement,

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:32.420
and are benefiting
from their product

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:35.080
and engineering teams' ability
to focus on tasks higher

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:37.130
in the tech stack.

00:02:37.130 --> 00:02:39.270
Matching qualified
candidates with the right job

00:02:39.270 --> 00:02:41.180
doesn't have to be so hard.

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:44.000
Let Google power your job
site with machine learning

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:47.330
and improve the discoverability
of jobs on your property.

00:02:47.330 --> 00:02:50.470
Learn more at cloud.google.com.

